---
// The problem Carton solves, before what the boundary holds. The figure is an
// app without Cartons: its files spill in a heap past a dashed outline where a
// box should be, and a patch in billing changes what shipping prints.
---

<section class="boundaries not-content" aria-labelledby="boundaries">
  <div class="copy">
    <h2 id="boundaries">Ruby, I love you<br class="phone-break" /> but we need<br class="phone-break" /> <span class="boxed">boundaries</span></h2>
    <p>Open classes and global constants are great until the app gets big. Then a money helper in Billing changes what Shipping prints.</p>
    <p>Linters miss what they can't parse. Services turn method calls into network calls. <strong>Carton draws the boundaries inside one process.</strong></p>
  </div>

  <figure class="heap" aria-label="An app without Cartons: billing patches Integer#to_s, so a shipping label prints Box $0.03 of $0.04; shipping calls Billing's internal ledger; and one Gemfile.lock pins faraday 1.10.6 while billing wants 2.x.">
    <div class="file">
      <p class="file-label">billing/core_ext.rb</p>
      <pre><code><span class="k">class</span> <span class="c">Integer</span>
  <span class="k">def</span> to_s = <span class="s">'$%.2f'</span> % (<span class="k">self</span> / <span class="m">100.0</span>)
<span class="k">end</span></code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="file">
      <p class="file-label">shipping/label.rb</p>
      <pre><code><span class="s">"Box #&#123;</span><span class="m">3</span><span class="s">&#125; of #&#123;</span><span class="m">4</span><span class="s">&#125;"</span>
<span class="x"># =&gt; "Box $0.03 of $0.04"</span></code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="file">
      <p class="file-label">shipping/ship.rb</p>
      <pre><code><span class="c">Billing</span>::<span class="c">Ledger</span>.post(order) <span class="o"># internals</span></code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="file">
      <p class="file-label">Gemfile.lock</p>
      <pre><code>faraday (<span class="s">1.10.6</span>) <span class="o"># Billing wants 2.x</span></code></pre>
    </div>
  </figure>
</section>

<style>
  .boundaries {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: 3rem 2rem;
  }

  /* Margins follow the hero's. */
  @media (max-width: 49.99rem) {
    .boundaries {
      padding-inline: 0.5rem;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 50rem) and (max-width: 67.99rem) {
    .boundaries {
      padding-inline: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    }
  }

  /* Desktop: the hero's two 32rem columns, the heap on the left. Below that,
     the heap follows the copy. */
  @media (min-width: 68rem) {
    .boundaries {
      grid-template-columns: 32rem 32rem;
      justify-content: center;
      column-gap: clamp(2rem, 100% - 64rem, 6rem);
      padding-block: 0 1.5rem;
    }

    .heap {
      order: -1;
    }
  }

  .copy {
    width: min(100%, 32rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 1.5rem + 2.5vw, 3.25rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-wrap: balance;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  /* Desktop sets the heading in two lines; phones break it as setup, turn,
     and the boxed word alone. */
  @media (min-width: 50rem) {
    .phone-break {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /* The word sits inside a boundary drawn like a Carton's: the hero's ruby
     tray, square to the page, against the heap's tilted cards. */
  .boxed {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 0.12em;
    padding: 0.02em 0.18em 0.1em;
    border: 0.05em solid var(--carton-ruby);
    border-radius: 0.22em;
    background: var(--carton-tray);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .copy p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
    line-height: 1.65;
    text-wrap: pretty;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }

  .copy p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .copy strong {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* The heap: cards tilted and overlapping, spilling past a dashed outline
     where a Carton's tray would be. */
  .heap {
    position: relative;
    width: min(100%, 32rem);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  }

  .heap::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 0;
    inset: 2.5rem 1.5rem;
    border: 1.5px dashed var(--carton-tray-edge);
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
  }

  .file {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    width: min(100%, 27rem);
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--carton-line);
    border-radius: 0.9rem;
    background: var(--carton-card);
    box-shadow: var(--carton-shadow);
  }

  .file + .file {
    margin-top: -0.6rem;
  }

  .file:nth-child(1) { rotate: -3deg; }
  .file:nth-child(2) { rotate: 2.5deg; align-self: flex-end; }
  .file:nth-child(3) { rotate: -1.5deg; margin-left: 1rem; width: min(100%, 29rem); }
  .file:nth-child(4) { rotate: 4deg; align-self: flex-end; margin-right: 2rem; width: min(100%, 22rem); }

  /* Phones: smaller tilts so the code stays readable and nothing clips. */
  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .heap {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
    }

    .file:nth-child(n) {
      rotate: 0deg;
      margin-inline: 0;
    }

    .file:nth-child(odd) { rotate: -1.5deg; }
    .file:nth-child(even) { rotate: 1.5deg; }
  }

  .file-label {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--carton-line);
    background: var(--carton-tab);
    color: var(--carton-ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--code-text);
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    white-space: pre;
  }

  pre code {
    padding: 0;
    background: none;
    font-size: inherit;
  }

  .k { color: var(--code-keyword); font-weight: 700; }
  .c { color: var(--code-constant); }
  .s { color: var(--code-string); }
  .m { color: var(--code-literal); }
  .o { color: var(--code-comment); }
  .x { color: var(--code-error); font-weight: 700; }
</style>
